<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0"><dict>
    <!-- DEMO BUILD ONLY — restored before any real/paid-team build.

         This file normally also declares:
           com.apple.developer.family-controls               (Screen Time shields)
           com.apple.developer.networking.networkextension   (Family DNS, dns-settings)
           com.apple.developer.usernotifications.time-sensitive

         All three are Apple-managed capabilities: a free Personal Team
         (RVDV9C73X4) cannot be issued them, so the device build failed with
         "Provisioning profile … doesn't include the Family Controls (Development)
         capability" and seven more like it. They are dropped here so the demo can
         be signed and installed on a real iPhone. The app already degrades
         honestly without them: DeviceControlsController.authorize() shows
         "Screen Time could not be enabled: …" rather than pretending success.

         Restore with:  git checkout -- ios/ClearView.entitlements -->
    <key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key><array><string>group.com.muddassir.clearview</string></array>
</dict></plist>
